  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that L-methioninate may interact with the sodium/bile acid cotransporter through a series of intermediate targets. Specifically, L-methioninate is directly linked to the splicing factor, proline- and glutamine-rich, which in turn is targeted by Npc112697 and Trichosanthoside A. Both of these compounds are also targets of Cercophorin B, which ultimately points to the sodium/bile acid cotransporter. This suggests a potential pathway where L-methioninate influences the activity of these splicing factors, which may then modulate the sodium/bile acid cotransporter. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a possible regulatory mechanism involving splicing factors and their downstream targets. The integration of these findings implies that L-methioninate could exert its effects through a network of molecular interactions that ultimately affect the sodium/bile acid cotransporter.",
